// Title: UAC Bypass via Windows Firewall Snap-In Hijack
// Sigma ID: e52cb31c-10ed-4aea-bcb7-593c9f4a315b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548
// Description: Detects attempts to bypass User Account Control (UAC) by hijacking the Microsoft Management
//   Console (MMC) Windows Firewall snap-in
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/uac-bypass-via-windows-firewall-snap-in-hijack.html#uac-bypass-via-windows-firewall-snap-in-hijack
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_hijacking_firwall_snap_in.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mmc.exe" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "WF.msc") and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\WerFault.exe"))
